{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc while image (resnet50, singleprofile) achieves only 20.8% acc, a gap of ~28 points. This raises a critical uncertainty: is the image modality fundamentally uninformative for this task, or is resnet50 simply an inadequate encoder? Question tested: config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) isolates the image encoder variable by swapping resnet50 for a much stronger pretrained ViT-L while keeping all other settings identical. Why this is the best next experiment: the result will determine the entire search direction. If ViT-L substantially improves image accuracy, multimodal fusion (configs 022-051) becomes a high-priority exploitation path. If it does not, the image modality is likely a dead end and budget should be redirected to RNA-only improvements (multiprofile, better encoders). With only 2 experiments completed, resolving this fork-in-the-road uncertainty is more valuable than incrementally improving the already-stronger RNA modality, as it effectively halves the remaining search space and prevents wasting budget on multimodal configs built on a weak image signal."
}

